/-!
# Axiom audit

`#print axioms` harness in the style of the formal-mathfin reference repo.
**Every public (non-`private`) named declaration of the development is
audited at every build**, so the proof-debt surface is machine-checked and
visible in the build log. The audit is exhaustive by construction: the list
below was generated by enumerating the `theorem`/`lemma`/`def`/`abbrev`/
`structure`/`instance` declarations of all 17 source modules and filtering
out `private` ones.

Exactly one class of declaration is out of reach and therefore absent: the
four ANONYMOUS `instance`s of the tree (`Definitions.lean` line 111,
`GaussianHelpers.lean` line 81, `CondExpBridge.lean` lines 110 and 113),
which have machine-generated names and cannot be cited by hand. Nothing else
is omitted. Auto-generated declarations (structure projections,
`.mk`/`.rec`/`.injEq`, instance fields) are likewise not listed; they are
derived from the audited parents.

`KyleUniqueness.Main` transitively imports the whole development except the
two leaf modules `BeyondPaper` and `IdentityTheoremSpike`, which are
imported here directly so that their declarations stay under audit.

## Expected output

405 `#print axioms` lines, every one of which must read

`depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.

`sorryAx` must not appear in any line of this file's build output.

## Status (final state after Session 3, waves 1–3, 2026-09-16)

**The formalization has NO open obligations.** There is no `sorry` anywhere
in the tree and no `axiom` declaration of our own. Session 3 closed the
value function (B1/B2 = v4 Lemma 2.4), the posterior (A1b/D1/D2 = v4
Lemma 2.1, §2.2, Lemma 2.5), the resampling measure (E1 = v4 Lemma 2.6),
the loss identities (v4 Lemmas 3.1/3.2), the accounting identity
(E2 = v4 Proposition 5.1), the signed root (H1), `1 ≤ 2Γ` (J1), the
saturation `Γ = 1/2` (T3 = v4 Proposition 6.1), the rigidity theorem
(N2 = v4 Theorem 7.1) and, in wave 3, the location–scale standardisation
(O1 = v4 §7), which carries the headline `isEquilibrium_eq_kyleStrategy`
(v4 Theorem 1.1, strategy half). Wave 3 also moved the six headline carriers
from `KyleUniqueness.Statement` to `KyleUniqueness.Main` and re-keyed every
module's docstrings from v3 to v4 numbering.

## Numbering

All paper references in this file are arXiv:2607.23585 **v4** (2026-08-20),
*The one-period Kyle model has one equilibrium*, except where explicitly
marked v3 or v2. Earlier sessions were keyed to v3; the crosswalk is
`STATEMENT_NOTES.md` §1 (policy:
`blueprint/LANE_C_DECISIONS_2026-09-16.md`, decision D1). Two references
below are deliberately NOT re-keyed because they have no v4 counterpart:
`SteinInequality.lean` formalizes **v3** Lemma 2.5 / v3 eq. (7), deleted in
v4, and `IdentityTheoremSpike.lean` serves a **v2** endgame deleted in v3.
-/

